  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "brief",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 900,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "OWEM · Phase 1 prototype — 20 screens, iOS system neutrals with the brand's acid lime spent exactly once per screen.\nStatic mockups for approval. Numbers are one consistent scenario: a $242.79 bill at Rosati's, five people, tax and tip split in proportion. Every share adds up to the total exactly."
    },
    {
      "id": "row-1",
      "x": -320,
      "y": 40,
      "w": 260,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "1 · START\nGet in, name the dinner, name the table. Nobody but the payer has an account."
    },
    {
      "id": "row-2",
      "x": -320,
      "y": 1044,
      "w": 260,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "2 · THE RECEIPT\nThe model reads it; you confirm it. Amber means a human still has to look — those lines cannot reach the maths."
    },
    {
      "id": "row-3",
      "x": -320,
      "y": 2048,
      "w": 260,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "3 · ASSIGN AND SETTLE\nWeights handle 'two of the three beers'. The settlement is locked and versioned — a correction writes v2, it never edits v1."
    },
    {
      "id": "row-4",
      "x": -320,
      "y": 3052,
      "w": 260,
      "page": "page-1",
      "text": "4 · COLLECT\nOWEM hands off to the rail with the amount filled in, then you confirm what landed. It never moves money and never marks anyone paid on its own."
    },
    {
      "id": "kit-note",
      "x": -320,
      "y": 40,
      "w": 260,
      "page": "page-2",
      "text": "Every screen is built from these. This is also the component list Phase 2 builds first, so the clickable build is assembly, not invention."
    }
  ],
